WEBVTT

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:27.930
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:27.930
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:27.930
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:53.100 --> 00:02:02.340
Chapter XI

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:10.100
The strange occurrence on Planet Econia came to an end two days later...

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:11.770
...which was sooner than
initially expected.

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:18.530
Commander Murai arrived one day ahead of schedule from Thanatos Military Police HQ.

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:55.650
According to the schedule weren't you supposed to arrive tomorrow, Commander Murai ?

00:02:56.170 --> 00:02:58.010
There was a
change of schedule.

00:02:58.010 --> 00:03:00.260
As abrupt as it may be,
I ask for your understanding.

00:03:01.190 --> 00:03:02.700
What the hell is
"a change of schedule" ?

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:05.320
It's how they planned
to do it, I'm sure.

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:08.160
It's nice to know that you're
so industrious at your job.

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:12.250
Since you are a wise officer, I'm sure you'll be
able to resolve this situation fairly and justly...

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:18.900
...without being influenced by the
false fame of the "Hero of El Facil."

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:24.030
Commander, we've prepared the 
conference room as your temporary office.

00:03:24.030 --> 00:03:25.640
You can use it anytime.

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:26.400
Okay.

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:30.880
First, LTJG Presberg, I will
start with your interrogation.

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:32.100
Commander Murai !

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:34.720
There's no need to talk
to someone like that !

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:38.510
That bastard, he's the fiendish criminal
who instigated this whole debacle...{disorder}

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:40.650
...and he only deserves
severe punishment !

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:49.100
I must inform you that I intend to gather a wide range of testimony from a wide range of witnesses, Captain.

00:03:49.690 --> 00:03:55.030
You never know what sort of false
allegations they might make for their own ends.

00:03:55.030 --> 00:03:58.440
They might lead
you to unfair biases.

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:03.250
I'm only trying to gather enough material in order to make a fair judgement.

00:04:03.250 --> 00:04:05.700
I have no biases.

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:10.410
Commander, aren't you forgetting
that my rank is Captain ?

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:12.700
Captain, there is something
you should not forget.

00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:16.450
That you are a party to this incident, and will
be on the receiving end of my interrogation.

00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:19.780
Till later.

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:35.480
Murai started his
investigation diligently.

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:39.350
His interrogation was thorough, and if he
found even a small conflict in the account...

00:04:39.350 --> 00:04:41.450
...he examined
those parts closely.

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:46.010
Lt. Commander Yang sided with a group of prisoners and instigated the revolt !

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:48.470
The truth of the
affair is obvious !

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:51.600
Lt. Patorichev participated in
this out of his own self-interest.

00:04:52.760 --> 00:04:54.960
Yang's position was tenuous.

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:58.480
If Headquarters were to accept
Captain Costea's assertions...

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:03.090
...his status would change from
"Hero of El Facil" to "Mutineer of Econia."

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:06.800
But Yang wasn't really concerned
about the gravity of the situation.

00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:11.310
Well, the two titles aren't all that different
since neither is a true reflection of myself.

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:15.400
That ridiculous lie that Lt. Commander Yang is an inspector from the Chief Staff Office...

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:17.860
...was cooked up by
Lt. Patorichev, wasn't it ?

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:20.210
He knows ?

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:21.390
I guess I should have known.

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:25.450
Well, it was a
matter of "expediency."

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:27.150
"Expediency" ?

00:05:27.570 --> 00:05:30.390
Murai was relentless in his interrogation on that point, but in other areas...

00:05:30.390 --> 00:05:33.980
...he listened conscientiously
to what the two had to say.

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:38.000
From what I've seen, Commander
Murai may lack originality...

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:41.770
...but he seems very capable in administrative issues and his judgement seems to be fair.

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:46.510
He's impersonal and censorious,
but I don't feel any malice from him.

00:05:47.190 --> 00:05:49.430
He seems to be
trustworthy, but...

00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:55.410
Then there is no evidence of Captain
Costea's embezzlement, is there ?

00:05:58.350 --> 00:06:02.100
In other words, you two just trusted
what a prisoner named Kefenhiller said...

00:06:02.100 --> 00:06:04.160
...and pointed a
gun at your superior ?

00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:09.570
But under the circumstances,
it all made sense, so...

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:13.130
With circumstantial evidence alone, you can't put a person on trial.

00:06:13.130 --> 00:06:14.780
But we've also got his confession...

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:19.310
A confession made under
duress is inadmissible in court.

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:23.310
Even if the confession were made willingly,
you cannot prove guilt on that basis alone.

00:06:23.310 --> 00:06:24.950
That's legal common sense.

00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:28.740
You two claim that your
actions were in self-defense.

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:33.010
But looking at it objectively, I have to say that your actions were quite imprudent.

00:06:36.610 --> 00:06:38.780
Commander Murai's investigation was swift.

00:06:38.780 --> 00:06:43.350
On the day of his arrival he interrogated all parties involved, and after the supper the same day...

00:06:43.350 --> 00:06:45.120
...he called all the
involved parties to his office.

00:06:46.530 --> 00:06:51.720
Captain Costea, we are arresting you on suspicion of public funds embezzlement.

00:06:53.610 --> 00:06:54.920
What kind of
farce is this ?!

00:06:54.920 --> 00:06:56.550
You didn't even do
a good investigation !

00:06:57.180 --> 00:07:01.970
I'm offended that you think I didn't
do anything before I came to Econia.

00:07:01.970 --> 00:07:05.660
I had already confirmed some facts
which I thought were necessary.

00:07:05.660 --> 00:07:11.550
For instance, about an anonymous
account in a bank on Phezzan.

00:07:16.350 --> 00:07:17.900
The Captain has lost.

00:07:17.900 --> 00:07:22.200
Commander Murai had already taken hold of the "trunk" of the issue before coming to Econia....

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:25.390
...and he only needed to search out the "branches" after his arrival.

00:07:26.610 --> 00:07:27.790
He's quite a competent person.

00:07:28.950 --> 00:07:34.600
You'll be held responsible for the deaths
of the guards and prisoners in this affair.

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:38.920
We will formally court-martial you at the
Thanatos Military Police Headquarters.

00:07:45.640 --> 00:07:46.870
Next, LTJG Presberg.

00:07:47.580 --> 00:07:49.200
Regardless of the circumstances...

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:53.390
...you illegally held Alliance officers
as hostages, even if only temporarily.

00:07:53.390 --> 00:07:56.550
But giving consideration to
Captain Costea's deception...

00:07:56.550 --> 00:07:59.520
...I sentence you to one
week of solitary confinement.

00:08:05.590 --> 00:08:10.650
Lt. Patorichev, since you made false testimony regarding Lt. Commander Yang's mission...

00:08:10.650 --> 00:08:12.100
...you will be reprimanded.

00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:14.580
But I will not leave that
in the official record.

00:08:14.580 --> 00:08:15.790
That is all for
these proceedings.

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:21.060
Um...how about me ?

00:08:22.190 --> 00:08:25.610
Regarding Lt. Commander Yang,
I see no reason for any punishment.

00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:28.200
But both Lt. Commander Yang
and Lt. Patorichev...

00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:32.200
...must be prepared to appear as
witnesses at Captain Costea's trial.

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:32.980
Yes, sir.

00:08:32.980 --> 00:08:34.360
I understand.

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:39.550
Lastly, regarding Captain Kefenhiller,
I also see no reason for any punishment.

00:08:39.550 --> 00:08:42.460
There are views that he was given
too much freedom of action...

00:08:42.460 --> 00:08:48.780
...but that is a supervisory issue for this
camp, and he cannot be held responsible.

00:08:49.470 --> 00:08:50.630
Any questions ?

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:55.080
That is all.

00:08:55.080 --> 00:08:55.950
You may go.

00:09:00.490 --> 00:09:01.610
That was handled excellently.

00:09:01.610 --> 00:09:05.410
I am someone who can only administrate according to the regulations.

00:09:06.200 --> 00:09:07.720
I can offer the
framework of regulations...

00:09:07.720 --> 00:09:11.430
...but I prefer leaving the task of administrating flexibly within that framework to others.

00:09:13.520 --> 00:09:15.790
He seems to be an
unexpectedly humble person.

00:09:21.940 --> 00:09:24.020
Though it cannot be said about the military organization as a whole...

00:09:24.020 --> 00:09:27.960
...I suppose there are many people who deserve trust or respect within the organization.

00:09:32.540 --> 00:09:36.530
Because of you, Lt. Commander, we were able to do a thorough cleaning of Planet Econia.

00:09:37.290 --> 00:09:39.180
I didn't do anything.

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:42.660
If someone should receive credit
for this, it has to be Mr. Kefenhiller.

00:09:43.450 --> 00:09:51.380
I suppose that old man is a savior to both of us, since he saved both our lives and our names.

00:09:51.380 --> 00:09:53.860
I feel that
debt will be huge.

00:09:54.630 --> 00:09:56.300
Well, shall we go thank him ?

00:10:02.340 --> 00:10:07.300
I plan to die an uninteresting death
on this uninteresting planet.

00:10:07.300 --> 00:10:15.200
I don't need this place to be like Valhalla, but if it's too dirty, it's not a nice residence, either.

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:18.300
So I thought I'd help a
bit with the cleaning.

00:10:19.260 --> 00:10:23.630
If there is anything I can do to
help you, please don't hesitate.

00:10:23.630 --> 00:10:27.440
After all, Captain,
you're our savior.

00:10:29.030 --> 00:10:31.610
Anything you can do, huh ?

00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:34.880
I suppose I shouldn't
expect too much, should I ?

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:44.040
Oh, can you send
LTJG Presberg back home ?

00:10:44.040 --> 00:10:49.220
Unlike me, that crybaby seems to be still longing for his mother's breasts.

00:10:50.800 --> 00:10:57.390
If that noisy boy is here,
I can't even take a peaceful nap.

00:10:57.390 --> 00:11:01.050
My hope is he'll leave soon
and be happy elsewhere.

00:11:01.050 --> 00:11:02.220
I understand.

00:11:02.220 --> 00:11:06.310
I don't have the authority myself, but
I will ask Commander Murai for a favor.

00:11:08.050 --> 00:11:10.550
Well, speak of the devil...

00:11:12.550 --> 00:11:18.250
"Captain Kefenhiller saved the lives of
Lt. Commander Yang and Lieutenant Patorichev."

00:11:18.250 --> 00:11:20.550
"Moreover, he made
considerable contributions..."

00:11:20.550 --> 00:11:24.210
"...to disclosing the wrongdoings that
were happening on Planet Econia."

00:11:24.210 --> 00:11:29.260
"To express gratitude for such actions, we are releasing the Captain from this POW camp."

00:11:29.260 --> 00:11:31.310
This is what I came
here to report.

00:11:31.310 --> 00:11:32.100
What ?

00:11:32.100 --> 00:11:34.190
Who asked for my release ?

00:11:34.190 --> 00:11:36.390
Don't bother making
such unnecessary trouble.

00:11:36.390 --> 00:11:39.100
I don't even want to return to
the Empire this late in my life.

00:11:39.100 --> 00:11:41.430
You have no obligations
to return home.

00:11:41.430 --> 00:11:43.370
You're free now.

00:11:45.390 --> 00:11:47.090
Free ?

00:11:48.700 --> 00:11:52.500
Freedom means doing what
one wants, doesn't it ?

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:57.550
Do you call it "freedom," to be assigned
a "freedom" that I didn't even want ?

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:04.330
Besides, it's not
like I have a job.

00:12:04.330 --> 00:12:06.720
If you put me on the street,
there's no way that I can make a living.

00:12:06.720 --> 00:12:09.950
If I stay in the camp, at least I don't have to worry about having enough to eat.

00:12:09.950 --> 00:12:15.230
Are you going to throw a jobless old man into the unkind waves of unsympathetic society ?

00:12:15.230 --> 00:12:18.340
Captain, your livelihood will be
guaranteed by the military.

00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:22.560
You will be given a pension at the
same rate of a retired Captain.

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:26.800
I'd like to demonstrate that our military
organization does have some compassion.

00:12:28.060 --> 00:12:29.670
{Human}"Compassion," huh ?

00:12:29.670 --> 00:12:35.460
I understand you may have your complaints,
but we shall resolve those at later time.

00:12:39.930 --> 00:12:43.490
Well, I never knew I'd
see such a rare spectacle.

00:12:44.560 --> 00:12:46.040
For Commander Murai to smile...

00:12:46.040 --> 00:12:47.230
...how should I say it...

00:12:47.230 --> 00:12:49.200
...a bronze statue is
breaking into a smile.

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:50.950
I never thought
it would happen.

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:55.410
I guess it means we shouldn't have
biases - it's a valuable life lesson.

00:12:59.340 --> 00:13:01.600
As a result of this,
Captain Kefenhiller...

00:13:01.600 --> 00:13:06.200
...had to leave Planet Econia, where
he had lived for over forty years.

00:13:06.200 --> 00:13:09.750
Hey, don't put those
books in that box.

00:13:09.750 --> 00:13:10.510
Yes, yes.

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:12.970
I'm thirsty.

00:13:12.970 --> 00:13:15.740
When you're done with
that, bring me some tea.

00:13:15.740 --> 00:13:17.200
Yes, I will.

00:13:17.200 --> 00:13:18.250
For Yang...

00:13:18.250 --> 00:13:22.510
...there were several things he wanted to learn while Kefenhiller was still on this planet.

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:26.750
Leaving the administrative
tasks to Murai...

00:13:26.750 --> 00:13:33.100
...Yang stayed with Kefenhiller to
satisfy his curiosity about history.

00:13:33.100 --> 00:13:37.350
But he was mostly helping to
pack Kefenhiller's belongings.

00:13:39.060 --> 00:13:42.610
By the way, you are
an eccentric man.

00:13:42.610 --> 00:13:49.630
During my time in this camp, I've seen 15 or so secretaries, but you interest me the most.

00:13:49.630 --> 00:13:53.140
The others were essentially
faultless but also meritless.

00:13:54.360 --> 00:13:57.820
We haven't known each
other that long, but still ?

00:13:57.820 --> 00:13:59.840
Meeting once is
more than enough.

00:13:59.840 --> 00:14:04.960
But of course, I'm not so conceited as to think
that I know everything about you already.

00:14:04.960 --> 00:14:10.550
Still, I think of you as
someone worthy of my interest.

00:14:11.680 --> 00:14:13.800
I'm flattered.

00:14:13.800 --> 00:14:16.500
Captain, I'm also very much interested
in finding out more about you.

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:19.230
That's good.

00:14:20.200 --> 00:14:22.360
Then let's start
with my story first.

00:14:26.230 --> 00:14:30.920
I was supposed to have spent an uneventful life as a bureaucrat in the Ministry of the Interior...

00:14:30.920 --> 00:14:34.900
...especially since my expertise
was in local governance.

00:14:34.900 --> 00:14:40.460
I would've been satisfied spending the rest
of my life as a mayor of a rural municipality.

00:14:40.460 --> 00:14:45.600
But that changed 48 years ago,
when I lost my wife.

00:14:45.600 --> 00:14:47.430
She passed away ?

00:14:48.330 --> 00:14:50.700
No, we parted alive.

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:52.910
But we didn't divorce, either.

00:14:56.100 --> 00:15:01.250
Our marriage was merely the result of
uniting two families of equal social status.

00:15:02.350 --> 00:15:07.800
For my part, though, I loved my wife
as a husband, and was faithful to her.

00:15:09.030 --> 00:15:13.940
But only one year into our marriage,
my wife asked for a divorce.

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:19.890
I found the right
path for my life.

00:15:20.150 --> 00:15:22.200
My wife was
having an affair.

00:15:23.800 --> 00:15:26.550
Her partner was the second
son of a Count's family...

00:15:26.550 --> 00:15:31.050
...who was beginning to gain
a reputation as an architect.

00:15:31.670 --> 00:15:34.370
It was a mistake to marry you.

00:15:34.990 --> 00:15:37.670
Let us go down
our chosen path.

00:15:37.670 --> 00:15:40.040
It would be an embarrassment
if you uselessly resist.

00:15:41.140 --> 00:15:45.650
As confused and troubled as I was,
I still refused to agree to a divorce.

00:15:46.280 --> 00:15:47.860
What a selfish man.

00:15:47.860 --> 00:15:51.110
After denouncing me,
my wife left.

00:15:52.480 --> 00:15:58.200
Her partner's brother initially tried to appease me and sent a large sum of money, but once I refused...

00:15:58.200 --> 00:16:07.550
...he changed tactics and tried to demote me to a rural area through his contacts in the Ministry.

00:16:09.200 --> 00:16:14.030
I was prepared for a rural assignment anyway, so I didn't yield.

00:16:14.030 --> 00:16:19.780
But when I heard that my wife and her
lover had had a child, I was devastated.

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:26.890
At that time, I was young enough to be able to despair at the ways of the universe.

00:16:26.890 --> 00:16:29.710
So I joined the military,
to seek my death.

00:16:30.870 --> 00:16:35.200
But after I became a prisoner,
my passion cooled down.

00:16:35.200 --> 00:16:39.550
I realized that if I died,
it would only make them happy.

00:16:39.550 --> 00:16:43.360
The fact that I'm alive -
that alone gives them trouble.

00:16:44.050 --> 00:16:46.100
It's such a distasteful thought.

00:16:46.100 --> 00:16:47.550
I'm aware of it myself.

00:16:48.150 --> 00:16:55.530
But as long as I live, my wife cannot get
a formal divorce, nor can she remarry.

00:16:55.530 --> 00:17:01.150
By remaining alive, I maintain
a tie with my homeland.

00:17:01.150 --> 00:17:04.750
Besides, if I'm alive...

00:17:04.750 --> 00:17:08.730
...I can be of some help to other people
once in a while, as I was just recently.

00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:12.850
That reminds me.

00:17:12.850 --> 00:17:15.370
Continuing our discussion
from that time, Captain...

00:17:15.370 --> 00:17:21.550
...am I correct that you sent the letter claiming that Admiral Bruce Ashbey's death was a murder plot ?

00:17:35.150 --> 00:17:39.090
As I thought, this old man doesn't seem to like direct questions.

00:17:40.190 --> 00:17:44.150
When you're out on the periphery frontier, you see the world around you...

00:17:44.150 --> 00:17:48.500
...and begin to recognize things that you couldn't see when you're right in the center of it all.

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:52.670
Or it could be just that you
feel like you can see it.

00:17:52.670 --> 00:17:56.680
So now, which culprit of which affair do you want to know about ?

00:18:00.100 --> 00:18:03.880
Um, I'm not particularly
interested in finding the culprit.

00:18:03.880 --> 00:18:10.100
I've always wanted to be a historian, and
I never thought about becoming a prosecutor.

00:18:11.920 --> 00:18:14.800
Basically, I just want
to know about things...

00:18:14.800 --> 00:18:20.680
...like the unsigned letter or the investigation assignment were only starting points for me.

00:18:21.310 --> 00:18:24.000
Um...I don't know
how to put it.

00:18:24.800 --> 00:18:29.800
People may say that I was
demoted to a do-nothing job...

00:18:29.800 --> 00:18:33.170
...but as far as I'm concerned,
I actually prefer it this way.

00:18:33.170 --> 00:18:34.300
And ?

00:18:34.300 --> 00:18:36.550
The plot to murder
Admiral Bruce Ashbey...

00:18:40.450 --> 00:18:43.310
...the defection of
Admiral Siegmeister...

00:18:43.310 --> 00:18:47.000
...the assassination
of Admiral Michaelsen.

00:18:47.000 --> 00:18:53.130
If a single thread connects these affairs that
spread from the Empire to the Alliance...

00:18:53.130 --> 00:18:57.840
...that thread must bear the name of an
espionage network, mustn't it, Captain ?

00:19:00.520 --> 00:19:02.270
That's the only way
I can make sense of it.

00:19:03.020 --> 00:19:08.030
For instance, the Imperial Intelligence office
would plan the murder of Bruce Ashbey.

00:19:09.030 --> 00:19:14.060
They would plant suspicion in the
Alliance politicians against Ashbey.

00:19:14.060 --> 00:19:18.370
Make them think that Ashbey's existence
was dangerous to the Alliance government.

00:19:18.370 --> 00:19:19.390
As a result....

00:19:21.380 --> 00:19:23.260
That's a highly likely scenario.

00:19:25.610 --> 00:19:31.890
I've gotten rather senile, and
I can't even remember what I said.

00:19:31.890 --> 00:19:34.650
Even if I said something...

00:19:34.650 --> 00:19:39.050
...it's dangerous to assume that I
sincerely believe in what I said, isn't it ?

00:19:39.350 --> 00:19:40.580
Yes, you're right.

00:19:41.990 --> 00:19:46.200
This old man doesn't seem inclined to
give me a straight answer any time soon.

00:19:46.200 --> 00:19:46.940
That's all right.

00:19:46.940 --> 00:19:49.650
I'll find the answers
myself and impress him.

00:19:53.250 --> 00:19:56.970
Well, we've had our rest,
so shall we resume packing ?

00:19:56.970 --> 00:19:58.370
Yes, yes.

00:20:02.100 --> 00:20:05.850
But I don't have much time left -
only till I'm done with this packing.

00:20:06.590 --> 00:20:13.080
But you actually believe there was a plot to
murder Admiral Bruce Ashbey, Lt. Commander ?

00:20:13.840 --> 00:20:15.640
I'm of two minds, actually.

00:20:15.640 --> 00:20:20.140
To be more precise, it's more
like 48 to 52, in favor of doubt.

00:20:20.140 --> 00:20:21.000
But of course...

00:20:21.000 --> 00:20:26.080
...I waver daily and half-daily, so I'm far
away from having any kind of conviction.

00:20:27.900 --> 00:20:30.550
I might be able to gather
circumstantial evidence...

00:20:30.550 --> 00:20:32.570
...but the same amount of
counter-evidence will gather, too.

00:20:32.570 --> 00:20:34.180
It's hard to say one way or the other.

00:20:34.180 --> 00:20:35.720
I see.

00:20:36.040 --> 00:20:39.700
Just because Bruce Ashbey didn't
have the holiest human attributes...

00:20:39.700 --> 00:20:42.460
...we can't disregard his
talents and accomplishments.

00:20:43.010 --> 00:20:46.550
Besides, people who accomplish
so much at such a young age...

00:20:46.550 --> 00:20:48.310
...aren't often meant to
maintain wholesome characters.

00:20:49.060 --> 00:20:50.460
The heroes of Dagon...

00:20:50.460 --> 00:20:56.460
...Fleet Admirals Limpao and Yusuf Tparl
weren't the kindest gentlemen either.

00:20:56.990 --> 00:21:03.450
But in any case, there are lots of low
characters with no talent in this world...

00:21:03.450 --> 00:21:07.420
...so it's remarkable that they
had at least one prominent side.

00:21:09.290 --> 00:21:12.040
Umm...as a general opinion,
I agree with you...

00:21:12.040 --> 00:21:16.260
...but I don't know if it's fair to conclude
that Ashbey was a disagreeable person.

00:21:16.260 --> 00:21:20.950
Even virtuous people can't
always be liked by everyone.

00:21:20.950 --> 00:21:22.720
You're right.

00:21:23.110 --> 00:21:26.040
Lt. Commander Yang, there's an
ultra high speed communication...

00:21:26.040 --> 00:21:28.960
...from the General Chief of
Staff Office on Heinessen.

00:21:30.600 --> 00:21:32.430
It's from someone
named Alex Cazellnu.

00:21:32.430 --> 00:21:33.150
Eh ?

00:21:39.310 --> 00:21:40.280
Hey, Yang.

00:21:40.280 --> 00:21:41.470
Commander !

00:21:41.470 --> 00:21:43.610
Sounds like you
had quite an adventure.

00:21:43.610 --> 00:21:47.650
I'll say it myself that I'm fortunate
not to suffer from boredom.

00:21:48.250 --> 00:21:50.800
I'm glad you're
not blaming me.

00:21:50.800 --> 00:21:55.310
Well, someone as capable as Commander Cazellnu can make mistakes sometimes.

00:21:55.310 --> 00:21:56.870
First, the news.

00:21:56.870 --> 00:22:01.450
It's been formally decided
that Admiral Alfred Rosas...

00:22:01.450 --> 00:22:04.790
...will be promoted to Fleet
Admiral on December 1st this year.

00:22:04.790 --> 00:22:06.800
That's good news.

00:22:06.800 --> 00:22:11.770
Admiral Rosas was worthy of the title of Fleet Admiral both in terms of his accomplishments and character.

00:22:12.730 --> 00:22:15.080
There is one more thing
that's been decided.

00:22:15.080 --> 00:22:16.660
You'll be summoned back.

00:22:17.330 --> 00:22:18.360
Huh ?

00:22:18.360 --> 00:22:23.430
Come back to Heinessen in
time for my wedding, all right ?

00:22:24.010 --> 00:22:26.500
Your journeyman life will have to be suspended for a while.

00:22:27.710 --> 00:22:30.260
As always, Commander
Cazellnu is brilliant.

00:22:30.260 --> 00:22:33.470
Taking reverse advantage of the
absurd trouble I was in as a rationale...

00:22:33.470 --> 00:22:37.100
...he arranged it so that I could
return to Heinessen immediately.

00:22:37.100 --> 00:22:39.660
He must have made
some shrewd moves.

00:22:40.610 --> 00:22:45.980
As a result, Lt. Commander Yang Wenli was
set to leave his post on Planet Econia.

00:22:45.980 --> 00:22:48.750
His appointment lasted
a mere two weeks -

00:22:48.750 --> 00:22:51.100
...a fact that dumbfounded him
more than anyone else.

00:22:51.100 --> 00:22:56.430
Though it was longer than his appointment as a Lieutenant, the comparison itself is absurd.

00:22:56.430 --> 00:22:57.750
In other words...

00:22:57.750 --> 00:23:03.490
...Yang broke the shortest appointment
record in the history of Econia as well.

